
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">During its earnings call, Apple advised that it is bracing for growing supply pressure on its products. I know some of this stems from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025–present_global_memory_supply_shortage">Ramageddon</a> and the massive build-out of AI server farms, but it feels like it runs deeper than that.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As Apple customers, we&#8217;ve always been accustomed to them just figuring it out and having a way to deliver their hardware despite market conditions. It sounds like that may be coming to an end. Just for giggles, I looked at the Apple Store this morning, and if I order a new stock 13&#8243; MacBook Air today, it will arrive in 2+ weeks.</p>



